{
  "dom_id": "step-q143564",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Given the joint probability distribution for two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ below, find $\\text{E}[X].$\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=-1$ | $0.05$ | $0.05$ | $0.2$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.15$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.15$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ |",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals, and the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals.\n\n| $f(x,y)$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=3$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=-1$ | $0.05$ | $0.05$ | $0.2$ | $0.3$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.15$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ | $0.4$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.15$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.3$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $…$ | $…$ | $…$ | $1$ |\n\nTherefore, the probability mass function for  $X$ is given by the following table:\n\n| $x$ | $-1$ | $1$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.3$ | $0.4$ | $0.3$ |\n\nFinally, the  expected value of $X$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}\\,{f}_{X}({x}_{i}) \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot 0.3+1\\cdot 0.4+3\\cdot 0.3 \\\\  & =-0.3+0.4+0.9 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
